====Usage notes====
Both {{m|en|surname}} and ''last name'' are extremely common terms for family names in all dialects of English. The former is somewhat more common in the UK and the latter in the US. Because of the cultural or gendered associations involved, however, it is increasingly common to prefer {{m|en|family name}} in multicultural or official contexts.

